 title="The Baudhāyana–Pythagoras Theorem",
 intro="In a right-angled triangle the square on the longest side equals the sum of the squares on the other two sides. This chapter builds the idea from doubling and halving squares, finds the length of the diagonal of a square, studies whole-number triples such as (3, 4, 5) and applies the theorem to solve problems.",
